# Base URL of the Konfidence API used by the browser fetch client.
#
# Defaults to `/api` (same-origin proxy) when unset. Set to a fully qualified
# URL (e.g. `https://api.konfidence.example`) when the API is hosted on a
# different origin.
#
# When set to a cross-origin URL the client automatically switches to
# `credentials: "include"`, so the API must respond with:
#   Access-Control-Allow-Origin: <this app's origin>
#   Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true
# and the browser must trust the API's TLS certificate.
#
# Local development typically uses the default and relies on the Vite proxy
# configured in `vite.config.ts` to reach the mock or real API.
# VITE_KONFIDENCE_API_BASE_URL=/api
